  "cues": [
    {
      "start": 0.26,
      "end": 2.52,
      "text": "A gecko can hold onto a wall."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.84,
      "end": 4.97,
      "text": "So how does it let go with every step?"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.48,
      "end": 7.76,
      "text": "The secret isn't just a strong grip."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.05,
      "end": 10.11,
      "text": "It's how that grip is controlled."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.79,
      "end": 15.67,
      "text": "Under a Tokay gecko's toes are tiny, hair-like structures called setae."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.23,
      "end": 19.97,
      "text": "Their branching tips make extremely close contact with the surface."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.56,
      "end": 22.15,
      "text": "They aren't suction cups."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.38,
      "end": 27.42,
      "text": "At that tiny scale, van der Waals forces help those tips adhere."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.42,
      "end": 28.72,
      "text": "But direction matters."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.12,
      "end": 33.97,
      "text": "A pull toward the base of the toe, along the surface, helps support the grip."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.4,
      "end": 38.17,
      "text": "To release, a gecko can curl its toes away from the surface."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.6,
      "end": 40.7,
      "text": "This movement helps the foot detach."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.32,
      "end": 44.65,
      "text": "That toe movement is called digital hyperextension."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.1,
      "end": 48.68,
      "text": "Don't confuse it with the angles of the microscopic hairs beneath it."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.26,
      "end": 52.4,
      "text": "So a gecko doesn't simply yank its foot off the wall."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.0,
      "end": 57.05,
      "text": "Close contact, the direction of loading, and controlled toe movement"
    },
    {
      "start": 57.05,
      "end": 60.5,
      "text": "work together to make gripping and letting go possible."
    }
  ]
}
